= Declarations and Bindings <ch:declarations>

== Syntax of Types

The special syntax for function, tuple and list types denotes the
built-in type constructors, and a parenthesized type is the type itself.

#translation-box[
  The following identities hold:
  #ottdrulefunXXtype()
  #ottdruletupleXXtype()
  #ottdrulelistXXtype()
  #ottdruleparenXXtype()
  where there are $k - 1$ commas in the tupling constructor.
]

== Strictness Flags

Whenever a data constructor is applied, each argument to the constructor
is evaluated if and only if the corresponding type in the algebraic
datatype declaration has a strictness flag, denoted by `!`.

#translation-box[
  A declaration of a constructor $K s_1 dots s_n$, where each $s_i$ is
  either of the form $! t_i$ or $t_i$, replaces every occurrence of $K$ in
  an expression as follows:
  #ottdrulestrictXXcon()
  Here $e_n$ is $(((K italic("op")_1 x_1) italic("op")_2 x_2) dots)
  italic("op")_n x_n$, and $italic("op")_i$ is the non-strict apply
  function `$` if $s_i$ is of the form $t_i$, and the strict apply function
  `$!` if $s_i$ is of the form $! t_i$.  The report writes $e_n$ directly;
  Ott cannot nest parentheses through an ellipsis, so it is a recurrence
  here.
]

